"Boudewijn Waijers" <kroisos@REMOVETHISWORD.home.nl> writes:
> Question for the source divers: when an egg is generated, is the monster
> level of the creature-to-be-born used to determine which eggs are
> eligable for that level, or is it the monster level of the
> creature-to-lay-the-egg?

Either. That is, if the random monster picked is either the baby or an
adult, you'll get an egg that will hatch into that baby; the game
tries 200 times to find one of these before giving up and making it a
generic non-hatchable egg (in the 1/3 chance that it was trying to
make a hatchable egg in the first place).

(There's further tweaks to make queen bee eggs and winged gargoyle
eggs rarer, since those are the "breeder" types for those species.)

